WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.000
Waldorf education is based on the principles of

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.580
Anthroposophy by Rudolf Steiner.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.140
Steiner founded the first school 
in 1919 Stuttgart Germany

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.340
to educate the children of the factory workers

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.540
from the Waldorf Astoria Zigaretten Fabrik

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:16.960
- hence the name.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.160
All kids, independent of social status or talent

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.860
received the same instruction,

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:26.140
which made the school a pioneer of social justice in education.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.680
The goal of a Waldorf education is to develop free,

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.880
but morally responsible individuals

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.420
equipped with a high degree of social competence

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.340
and creative capabilities.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.780
Factual knowledge,

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.960
homework and tests scores receive less attention.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.940
Storytelling and experimentation

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.340
are the main method of instruction,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.540
Over the twelve-year curriculum,

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.020
students learn math,

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:51.940
literature,

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.220
history and science

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.700
as well as a wide variety of arts and hands-on skills.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.860
Elementary students paint,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:00:59.580
knit,

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.780
weave and sculpt with wax.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.720
Older ones make patterns,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:04.560
books,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.080
pottery and sculpt in stone.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.520
Everybody learns to do music.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.380
First all play the flute,

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.080
then some play string instruments

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.820
and others join the choir.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.760
Students play non-competitive games

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.740
and learn to dance eurhythmy.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.420
They do organic farming

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.420
and learn two foreign languages,

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.760
which in the first years are taught through songs,

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.000
storytelling and conversations.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.080
In grade 8 and 12

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.820
the entire class develops a classical drama

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.020
which they perform in front of their parents and friends.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.220
Waldorf uses a unique

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.160
project based approach to almost

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.360
all main academic subjects.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.180
Instead of repetitive schedules,

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.560
a specific subject,

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:48.780
such as history,

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.580
math,

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.180
science or even gardening

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.240
dominates the first two hours in the morning

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:55.640
for a period of 4-6 weeks.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:58.580
After that, a new subject gets the main focus.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:04.020
Steiner also invented an experiential 
approach to science

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.500
whereby students observe

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.780
and later describe scientific concepts

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.720
in their own words and drawings

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.760
rather than learning about them in a textbook first.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.620
Waldorf schools therefore consider computers

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.140
useful to children only in their teens,

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.260
after they have mastered fundamental,

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.920
time-honored ways of discovering

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.580
information and learning.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.100
In the spirit of personal development and empathy,

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.740
competition and grades are being avoided.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.540
Teachers instead assess the student’s individual

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.020
growth of character.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.120
Tests scores and grades are only slowly introduced to

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.220
older students as they prepare for college

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.940
and entrance exams.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:44.880
Today there are over

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.780
a thousand Waldorf schools in 60 countries,

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.760
making it one of the largest independent

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.100
school movements.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.060
Waldorf has become a recognized

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.120
educational theory in Europe

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.980
and its schools have received state funding.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:02.480
Famous Waldorf parents include Clint Eastwood,

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.520
Lenny Kravitz,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.760
the Forbes family

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.620
and many parents from Silicon Valley’s tech sector

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.020
despite Steiner’s critical view of technology

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.520
and mass media.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.980
Steve Jobs once told a tech journalist

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.560
who asked whether his children like the new iPad

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.720
that they haven’t used it and continued:

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.420
“We limit how much technology our kids use at home.”

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.240
Acclaimed psychiatrist William Glasser famously said

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.600
that we learn 10% of what we read,

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.660
20% of what we hear,

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.440
30% of what we see,

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.020
but 80% of what we experience.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.960
one could argue that despite their low-tech approach,

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.660
the experimental learning method of

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:44.300
Waldorf education is exceptionally contemporary.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.000
What do you think?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.100
